<a href="https://github.com/AJBogo9/ulauncher-math-symbols" class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm">GitHub</a>

Type `m sum` in [Ulauncher](https://ulauncher.io), press Enter, and ∑ is on the clipboard.

<video src="demo.mp4" autoplay loop muted playsinline controls aria-label="Searching m alpha, m sigma and m gamma in Ulauncher, then opening the copy actions for γ with Alt+Enter" style="display:block; width:100%; height:auto; margin:0 0 1.25rem; border-radius:8px;"></video>

The extension finds a symbol by its LaTeX name (`\mathbb{R}` for ℝ), a nickname (`expectation` for 𝔼) or words of its Unicode name (`not equal` for ≠).

It needs Ulauncher 6 (still in beta). To install it, open Extensions in Ulauncher's preferences, click Add extension and paste the GitHub link.
